/Creator (H Heuristics)
/Keywords (polycrisis resilience\054 polycrisis\054 systemic risk\054 cascading risks\054 adaptive capacity\054 disaster risk reduction\054 climate adaptation\054 sustainable development\054 development economics\054 planetary boundaries\054 resilience measurement)
/ModDate (D\07220261104201138\05505\04700\047)
/Producer (ReportLab PDF Library \055 www\056reportlab\056com)
/Subject (Humanity\220s major challenges increasingly interact through complex networks of environmental\054 economic\054 technological and societal risks\054 a condition commonly described as a polycrisis\056 Existing approaches to resilience\054 disaster risk reduction\054 climate adaptation and sustainable development each address important dimensions of this challenge but are often organized around individual hazards or systems\056 This report introduces Polycrisis Resilience\054 a proposed framework developed by H Heuristics to describe and strengthen the capacity of individuals\054 communities\054 economies\054 institutions and interconnected systems to anticipate\054 withstand\054 adapt to\054 recover from\054 and reduce the cascading and compounding effects of multiple interconnected crises\056)
/Title (Polycrisis Resilience\072 Defining the Capacity to Withstand\054 Adapt to and Reduce the Interconnected Risks of the 21st Century)
/Trapped /False
>>
